  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "ONNX inference release. `export onnx --kv-cache` adds per-layer past/present key-value tensors so autoregressive generation runs O(1) per token instead of re-processing the whole sequence (~4.8x faster at 200 tokens); one graph serves both prefill and incremental decode. fp16 quantized export now executes natively in half precision (weights, activations, and RoPE tables all fp16, with norms in an fp32 sandwich and logits cast back to fp32) rather than dequantizing to fp32 at load, so the memory saving is real on fp16-capable providers. Generation is hardened: KV-cache models stop at the model's context length, empty prompts are rejected with a clear error, and over-long prompts fail up front instead of crashing deep in tensor indexing. The ONNX backend auto-detects a KV-cache graph and decodes incrementally.",
